<div id="notes gs2"></div><sup>2</sup><small> Includes cup competitions: the [[Glasgow Cup]], [[Drybrough Cup]] and the [[Anglo-Scottish Cup]]. Appearance and goal statistics are not readily available for the [[Glasgow Merchants Charity Cup|Glasgow Charity Cup]]</small>

<div id="notes gs3"></div><sup>3</sup><small> In addition to these statistics, it is known that McGrory made a further 21 appearances in the Glasgow Charity Cup, scoring 20 goals. This makes McGrory's overall total of goals for Celtic in senior competitions 522 goals</small><ref name="jim550">{{cite book|last=Cairney|first=John|title=Heroes are Forever: The Life and Times of Celtic Legend Jimmy McGrory|date=2007|publisher=Mainstream Publishing|isbn=9781780570617|chapter-url=https://books.google.com/books?id=yOT7E7NGfB4C&q=jimmy+mcgrory+glasgow+charity+cup+goals&pg=PT78|chapter=McGrory statistics}}</ref>

===International===
*First capped player: [[Willie Groves]] and [[Thomas McKeown (footballer)|Thomas McKeown]] (for [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]], against [[Ireland national football team (1882&ndash;1950)|Ireland]], 9 March 1889)<ref>{{cite web|title=Scotland caps (Celtic)|url=http://londonhearts.com/scotland/clubs/celtic.html#GamesbyDate|publisher=London Hearts Supporters Club|accessdate=1 March 2016}}</ref>
*Most international [[cap (sport)|caps]] while a Celtic player: [[Packie Bonner]], 80 for [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]]<ref name="capsceltic">{{cite book|last=McGuirk|first=Brian|title=Celtic FC - the Ireland Connection|date=April 2009|publisher=Black and White Publishing|isbn=978-1845022488|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=Ah0jAwAAQBAJ&q=pat+bonner+most+appearances+celtic&pg=PT155|accessdate=28 September 2015}}</ref>
*Most international [[cap (sport)|caps]] for [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]] while a Celtic player: [[Paul McStay]], 76<ref name="capsceltic" />
*Most [[cap (sport)|capped]] player to play for Celtic: [[Robbie Keane]], 143 for [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]] (3 caps whilst at Celtic){{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*Most international goals while a Celtic player: [[Henrik Larsson]], 21 for [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]]{{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}

====World Cup====
*First Celtic player to appear at a [[FIFA World Cup|World Cup]]: [[Willie Fernie (footballer)|Willie Fernie]] and [[Neil Mochan]] (for [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]] against [[Austria national football team|Austria]] 8 June 1954){{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*First Celtic player to score at a World Cup: [[Bobby Collins (footballer)|Bobby Collins]] (for [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]], against [[Paraguay national football team|Paraguay]], 11 June 1958){{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*Most [[FIFA World Cup|World Cup]] appearances while a Celtic player: [[Packie Bonner]], 9{{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*Most World Cup goals while a Celtic player: [[Henrik Larsson]], 5{{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*First World Cup winner to play for Celtic: [[Juninho Paulista|Juninho]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.freepubquiz.co.uk/celtic-football-quiz.html|title=Celtic Football Quiz, Celtic Football Trivia|work=FreePubQuiz}}</ref>

====European Championship====
*First Celtic player to appear at a [[UEFA European Football Championship|European Championship]]: [[Packie Bonner]], [[Mick McCarthy]] and [[Chris Morris (footballer)|Chris Morris]] (for [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]], against [[England national football team|England]], 12 June 1988){{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*First Celtic player to score at a European Championship: [[Paul McStay]] for [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]], against [[CIS national football team|CIS]], 18 June 1992)
*Most [[UEFA European Football Championship|European Championship]] appearances while a Celtic player: [[Henrik Larsson]], 7{{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}
*Most European Championship goals while a Celtic player: [[Henrik Larsson]], 4{{Citation needed|date=May 2017}}

